Hestia: Ah, welcome, Aelius dear. Are you ready to begin the day?
Aelius: I suppose so. I think I’m starting to get the hang of your routine.
Hestia: Well… today might throw you off a little bit.
Aelius: … What’s that supposed to mean?
Aelius: Is there something different going on today?
Hestia: You could say that, yes.
Hestia: Seeing how you’ve had a rather positive impact on the Olympians, I invited a few of the others today.
Hestia: I asked Hera, Ares, and Aphrodite if they would come in together.
Hestia: They have some issues with each other and some of the other Olympians, so I thought you might be able to try and talk to them.
Aelius: I don’t know… I’m not sure how I could help them. I’m just starting to get to know them and their issues.
Aelius: Besides, I’m just a mortal – why would they listen to me?
Aelius: Especially Ares, he’s arrogant and rude. I don’t think he would even give me a chance.
Hestia: I think you'll be able to do more than you think.
Hestia: You haven’t spent all your life up here like the others and I.
Hestia: I think you having a fresh perspective will do wonders for change.
Aelius: You really think so?
Hestia: My dear, I know you can.
Hestia: Oh, as for Ares being… difficult, all you need to do is provide an incentive for him.
Hestia: I hear he really enjoys sweets, so use that as you see fit.
Aelius: [Positive] Heh, for such an intimiating guy, I hadn't expected that.
Hestia: Like I said, you have everything you need to help be the change we all need, so got this.
Aelius: [Positive] Thanks Hestia!
Hestia: Ah! Here comes Hera now.

